VALUES ('Nelly', 'Nelly', 'nelly', 'Male', 'Sound', '1974-11-02', NULL, 'Austin, Texas, USA', 'Cornell Iral Haynes Jr. (born November 2, 1974), known professionally as Nelly, is a multi-Grammy Award-winning American rapper, singer, and actor. Ranked as one of the best-selling rap artists in American music history, his diamond-certified debut album Country Grammar (2000) and multi-platinum follow-up Nellyville (2002) yielded timeless worldwide number-one smashes like \"Hot in Herre\", \"Dilemma\" (featuring Kelly Rowland), \"Ride wit Me\", and \"Just a Dream\". As an actor, he starred as Earl Megget in the hit sports comedy The Longest Yard (2005).', 'people/photos/nelly.jpg', 'https://www.instagram.com/nelly', '{\"instagram\":\"https:\\/\\/www.instagram.com\\/nelly\",\"twitter\":\"https:\\/\\/twitter.com\\/Nelly_Mo\",\"imdb\":\"https:\\/\\/www.imdb.com\\/name\\/nm1027137\\/\"}', 1, 'active', 1, @now, @now)
