VALUES ('Monali Thakur', 'Monali Thakur', 'monali-thakur', 'Female', 'Sound', '1985-11-03', NULL, 'Kolkata, West Bengal, India', 'Monali Thakur (born 3 November 1985) is an Indian playback singer and actress. Renowned for her emotive vocal sweetness, Thakur won the prestigious National Film Award for Best Female Playback Singer for the timeless romantic ballad \"Moh Moh Ke Dhaage\" from Dum Laga Ke Haisha (2015). She also won the Filmfare Award for Best Female Playback Singer for the sensational hit \"Sawaar Loon\" from Lootera (2013). Her other smash hits include \"Zara Zara Touch Me\" (Race) and \"Cham Cham\" (Baaghi). As an actress, she received critical acclaim for Nagesh Kukunoor\'s drama Lakshmi (2014).', 'people/photos/monali-thakur.jpg', 'https://www.instagram.com/monalithakur03', '{\"instagram\":\"https:\\/\\/www.instagram.com\\/monalithakur03\",\"twitter\":\"https:\\/\\/twitter.com\\/monalithakur03\",\"imdb\":\"https:\\/\\/www.imdb.com\\/name\\/nm3863495\\/\"}', 1, 'active', 1, @now, @now)
