VALUES ('Anna Wintour', 'Dame Anna Wintour', 'anna-wintour', 'Female', 'Production', '1949-11-03', NULL, 'Hampstead, London, England, UK', 'Dame Anna Wintour (born 3 November 1949) is a British-American media executive and global fashion icon who has served as the Editor-in-Chief of American Vogue since 1988 and Global Chief Content Officer for Condé Nast. Widely regarded as the most powerful figure in world fashion, she is the principal organizer and visionary behind the prestigious annual Met Gala in New York. Her trademark pageboy bob haircut and dark sunglasses made her a cultural icon, and she served as the inspiration for the character Miranda Priestly in the hit film The Devil Wears Prada.', 'people/photos/anna-wintour.jpg', 'https://www.vogue.com', '{\"imdb\":\"https:\\/\\/www.imdb.com\\/name\\/nm0936004\\/\"}', 1, 'active', 1, @now, @now)
